    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d855">

                <pb facs="0754" n="742" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg742"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M)/7209: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Steinhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ankara</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-06-13T18:00:00+03:00">June 13, 1942—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 14—1:47 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>598. My 574, June 11, 5 p.m. British Ambassador informed me yesterday
                        Saraçoğlu<anchor n="71" xml:id="d855-f1"/> had expressed readiness of
                    Turkish Government to enter into negotiations for a new Anglo-Turkish chrome
                    agreement.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d855-f1" n="71" xml:id="d855-f1-content">
                <p>Sükrü Saraçoğlu, Turkish Minister for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
